we receive your name, email address, profile picture, and tokens to authenticate API access to your Google Drive and Google Sheets.\n\u2022 Call Recordings (Audio): Audio files stored on your device that you grant access to via Android Storage Access Framework. Audio files are NEVER uploaded to or stored on our servers.\n\u2022 Call Metadata: File names, durations, timestamps, and caller details matched from your local device call logs to organize records and sync with your connected Google Sheet.\n\u2022 Transcripts & AI Summaries: Text transcripts and analysis generated via speech-to-text APIs. Stored locally on your device and inside your designated personal Google Sheet or Google Drive folder.\n\n2. THIRD-PARTY SERVICES & AI PROCESSING\n\u2022 Google OAuth & APIs: Used with restricted scopes (drive.file and spreadsheets) to create and access only files generated by this application.\n\u2022 Speech-to-Text & AI APIs: When you initiate transcription or enable background processing queues, audio snippets are submitted to the configured API for transcription and summarization.\n\u2022 Zero Data Selling: We do not sell, rent, or lease your personal data, audio recordings, or transcripts to any third-party broker or advertiser.\n\n3. DATA RETENTION & SECURITY\n\u2022 Device-First Architecture: Recordings remain on your physical device and in your personal cloud accounts.\n\u2022 Security: Authentication tokens are secured using Android Keystore-backed encrypted storage.\n\u2022 Deletion: You can delete recordings, clear app cache, or sign out at any time. Revoke Google access anytime via your Google Account Permissions.\n\n4. CONTACT & INQUIRIES\nFor privacy inquiries, help, or support: prajwalnair2603@gmail.com":'terms'===o?"Last updated: September 25, 2026\nEffective Date: September 25, 2026\n\nBy installing or using Audify AI, you agree to these Terms & Conditions.\n\n1. ELIGIBILITY & ACCEPTANCE\n\u2022 You must be at least 18 years of age (or legal age in your jurisdiction) to use this application.\n\u2022 You agree to use the application solely for lawful business management and personal organizational purposes.\n\n2. COMPLIANCE WITH CALL RECORDING LAWS (CRITICAL)\n\u2022 User Sole Responsibility: Laws governing telephone recording consent vary by jurisdiction (one-party vs. all-party/two-party consent).\n\u2022 Consent Obligation: You warrant and represent that you have obtained all required consents from all parties on every call before recording or importing audio.\n\u2022 Indemnification: Audify AI disclaims all liability for unlawful or non-consensual recordings. You agree to indemnify and hold harmless Audify AI and its operators from any legal actions or claims arising from violation of recording statutes.\n\n3. AI ACCURACY & RELIANCE DISCLAIMER\n\u2022 Automated Technology: Transcription, sentiment analysis, and summaries are generated by automated artificial intelligence models.\n\u2022 No Warranty of Accuracy: Output may contain errors, omissions, or misinterpretations due to audio quality, speech accents, or model limitations.\n\u2022 Verification Required: Transcripts must be independently verified by a human before relying on them for legal, financial, medical, or high-stakes business decisions.\n\n4. THIRD-PARTY APIS & BILLING\n\u2022 If you provide your own API keys or endpoints, you are solely responsible for usage costs, rate limits, and compliance with the terms of those providers.\n\n5. PROHIBITED USES\n\u2022 Unlawful surveillance, wiretapping, stalking, or harassment.\n\u2022 Reverse-engineering, decompiling, or redistributing the application.\n\u2022 Uploading malicious code or infringing intellectual property.\n\n6. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY\n\u2022 Audify AI is provided \"AS IS\" and \"AS AVAILABLE\" without warranties of any kind. To the maximum extent permitted by law, liability is limited strictly to amounts paid, if any.":"Responsible Use Guidelines for Audify AI:\n\n\u2705 DO:\n\u2022 Always notify and obtain explicit consent from all call participants before recording or transcribing.\n\u2022 Review and verify AI transcripts manually before taking consequential business or legal actions.\n\u2022 Regularly back up recordings to your personal Google Drive and delete unneeded device files.\n\u2022 Protect sensitive customer information by restricting access to your exported Google Sheets.\n\u2022 Use Wi-Fi connections when performing large batch uploads to avoid mobile data charges.\n\n\u274c DON'T:\n\u2022 NEVER record or transcribe phone calls in violation of local consent laws.\n\u2022 Do not process or transcribe sensitive financial credentials (credit cards, CVVs), passwords, or protected medical data without appropriate compliance controls.\n\u2022 Do not share exported transcripts containing confidential customer information with unauthorized third parties.\n\u2022 Do not rely on automated AI sentiment or summaries as definitive legal or employment records without human corroboration.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 AI SPEECH RECOGNITION NOTES:\n\u2022 Background noise, low call volume, and heavy accents may reduce transcription accuracy.\n\u2022 Always treat initial AI output as an unverified draft.\n\n\ud83d\udcf1 STORAGE & BACKUP TIPS:\n\u2022 Designate your exact phone call recording folder in Settings.\n\u2022 Manage local device storage regularly as recordings are preserved until manually deleted.\n\nSupport & Inquiries: prajwalnair2603@gmail.com"),isChecked:h[e.id],onCheck:()=>I(e.id)},e.id);var o}),(0,s.jsxs)(r.View,{style:u.disclaimer,children:[(0,s.jsx)(n.default,{name:"information-outline",size:14,color:_r(d[7]).Colors.textTertiary}),(0,s.jsx)(r.Text,{style:u.disclaimerText,children:"By continuing, you confirm you are 18 years or older and have the authority to accept these terms on behalf of your organization."})]}),(0,s.jsx)(r.TouchableOpacity,{style:[u.continueBtn,A?u.continueBtnActive:u.continueBtnDisabled],onPress:T,disabled:!A||S,activeOpacity:.85,acce